<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#manuscript-illumination">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuscript illumination</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">Manuscript</a> illumination is the decoration of handwritten books with painted images, ornament and gold. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, Persian illumination and painting absorbed Chinese influences, producing works such as illustrated histories and copies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahnameh">Shahnameh</a>. This art laid foundations for the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">Persian miniature</a> tradition.</p></div>
